foundation.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,1.60) {Cement};
\foreach \x in {0.00} {\draw[fill=blue!15] (\x,1.30) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.95) {Sand};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70} {\draw[fill=red!12] (\x,0.65) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.30) {Gravel};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40,2.10} {\draw[fill=green!20] (\x,0.00) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,amplitude=5pt}] (3.05,1.90)--(3.05,0) node[midway,right=8pt,font=\small] {$350$ kg};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Concrete is made from cement, sand and gravel in the ratio $1:2:4$. How much of each is needed to make a $350$ kg batch of concrete?

foundation.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,1.60) {Cement};
\foreach \x in {0.00} {\draw[fill=blue!15] (\x,1.30) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (0.35,1.60) {$50$};
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.95) {Sand};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70} {\draw[fill=red!12] (\x,0.65) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\foreach \x in {0.35,1.05} {\node[font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0.95) {$50$};}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.30) {Gravel};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40,2.10} {\draw[fill=green!20] (\x,0.00) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\foreach \x in {0.35,1.05,1.75,2.45} {\node[font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0.30) {$50$};}
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,amplitude=5pt}] (3.05,1.90)--(3.05,0) node[midway,right=8pt,font=\small] {$350$ kg};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$7\text{ parts}=350\text{ kg}$
$1\text{ part}=50\text{ kg}$
$2\text{ parts}=100\text{ kg}$
$4\text{ parts}=200\text{ kg}$
The batch needs $50$ kg of cement, $100$ kg of sand and $200$ kg of gravel.

